From: Roy <me@dwroy.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:36:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bound the fixed illusion rollout regression

Migrate the ZY3992X5VEVS floor 23 turn 3-5 planner assertion to an
isolated suite using committed model fixtures and the existing work
clock. Restore the 1500 ms rollout budget instead of 1e9, preserve all
ranking and target-order assertions, and require multiple samples to
reach turns 4 and 5 within a bounded amount of solver work.

Evidence: fix-queue-v4 batch-c-fixed-fixture-timeout, host check
20261012-183755-s2-strategy-proposal (17210 ms at a 15000 ms test limit).
The original timeout and its passing targeted supplement remain valid;
this change does not claim to establish the historical host pause cause.
No production mechanics, character knowledge or timeout limits change.

Reverting the fixture clock/budget makes both new cases fail (376 policy
turns or wall-clock leakage); restoring it passes both pause scenarios
and the related fixed regressions. Sandbox coverage passes (342 files,
3408 cases) with tsc and gitleaks. Preserve the initial import-check
failure from source snapshots in learner/runs; archive those as text
and continue only check-imports and the previously unrun paths suite.

